From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:17:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: drop duplicate newline from infoframe log message

NV_DRM_LOG_INFO() already appends "\n" to the format string, so the
"Infoframe changed on CRTC ..." message added in 615.71.09 (61dcc937)
was followed by an empty line in the kernel log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index 06f39b32..479f0e33 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -704,7 +704,7 @@ int nv_drm_atomic_check(struct drm_device *dev,
 
                 /* Check if HDR metadata or colorspace changed */
                 if (hdr_changed || colorspace_changed || vsif_metadata_changed) {
-                    NV_DRM_LOG_INFO("Infoframe changed on CRTC %d (hdr=%d colorspace=%d vsif=%d), adding planes on CRTC to atomic commit\n",
+                    NV_DRM_LOG_INFO("Infoframe changed on CRTC %d (hdr=%d colorspace=%d vsif=%d), adding planes on CRTC to atomic commit",
                            to_nv_crtc(crtc)->head,
                            hdr_changed,
                            colorspace_changed,
